    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d405">

                <pb facs="0901" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1951v04p1/pg859"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 405</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">752.00/2–2351: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Spain
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d405-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-02-23T19:00:00-05:00">February 23,
                            1951—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>539. Brit Emb states FonOff understands Franco may sound out US and UK Ambs re
                    attitudes their govts if he “broadens base” his regime. FonOff thinks this
                    maneuver connected Franco’s negots with Monarchists since it is informed Franco
                    may meet soon with Don Juan.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d405-f2"/> Brit believes
                    maneuver cld have two purposes: 1) favor Monarchists over other opposition
                    groups thus possibly driving latter into hands Commies; 2) involve US and UK
                    Embs in domestic Span polit intrigues.</p>
                <p> FonOff instructing Brit Amb, if approached, give no indication type regime UK
                    wld like see estab Spain and restrict his remarks to saying simply Brit Govt wld
                    like see Spain play its full role Western Eur community but believes this will
                    be difficult unless regime is “liberalized”.</p>
                <p> FonOff instructed Emb ask us instruct Amb Griffis similarly, in interest
                    maintaining common policy re Spain, informed Emb we had no info this subj but
                    wld inquire. Please advise.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d405-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d405-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Dunham, cleared and initialed over Secretary Acheson’s signature by
                    Williamson, and repeated to London.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d405-f2" n="2" xml:id="d405-f2-content">
                <p>Pretender to the Spanish Throne.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
